description:
Write a small CSV toolkit in a static class `Csv`:

```csharp
public static List<string> ParseLine(string line)
public static string FormatLine(IEnumerable<string> fields)
public static Dictionary<string, decimal> TotalsBy(TextReader reader, string keyColumn, string valueColumn)
public static async Task<int> CopyColumnsAsync(string inputPath, string outputPath, params string[] columns)
```

- `ParseLine` splits on commas, except inside double quotes. Inside quotes, `""` stands for one `"`. `a,"b, c","say ""hi"""` gives `a`, `b, c`, `say "hi"`. An empty line gives one empty field.
- `FormatLine` does the reverse: fields containing a comma, a quote or a line break are quoted, with quotes doubled.
- `TotalsBy` reads CSV with a header row from any `TextReader`, and sums `valueColumn` (an invariant-culture decimal) per value of `keyColumn`. A missing column throws `ArgumentException`. Blank lines are skipped.
- `CopyColumnsAsync` reads a CSV file and writes a new one with only the named columns, in the order given (header included), and returns the number of data rows written. A missing input file lets the `FileNotFoundException` through.

